<title>RUSSIA: WEATHER - Conditions at CIS airports - November 4.</title>
<headline>WEATHER - Conditions at CIS airports - November 4.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thick morning fog may force Moscow's four airports to postpone flights on November 5, the Russian Weather Service said on Monday.</p>
<p>The airports face a 70 percent chance of closure, it said.</p>
<p>Strong winds, low clouds and wet snow may close airports in the Magadan and Khabarovsk regions, the Kurile islands and the Kamchatka peninsula in the Russian Far East on November 5 and 6, the service said.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
